ces: Rams' Puka Nacua out 4-5 months after knee surgery, will miss playoffs","description":"Puka Nacua's recovery time from MCL surgery is considered to be four to five months, sources told ESPN, meaning he will miss the playoffs.","published":"2026-11-22T02:19:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50556613/sources-rams-puka-nacua-4-5-months-knee-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Schefter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football Week 11 inactives: Who's in and who's out?","description":"Updated inactives and analysis based on the latest reports and official announcements leading up to kickoff.","published":"2026-11-21T20:32:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFSundayInactives-50530832/fantasy-football-injuries-nfl-week-11-inactive-active","type":"Story","byline":"Michael F. Florio","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cardinals rule out rookie Carson Beck, turn to 40-year-old Josh Johnson vs. Chiefs","description":"Cardinals rookie quarterback Carson Beck has been downgraded to out, paving the way for 40-year-old Josh Johnson to start against the Chiefs.","published":"2026-11-21T21:41:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50553035/cardinals-downgrade-qb-carson-beck-josh-johnson-set-start","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Josh Weinfuss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Steelers activate WR Roman Wilson off IR for Eagles game","description":"The Steelers have activated wide receiver Roman Wilson from injured reserve ahead of Sunday's game against the Eagles.","published":"2026-11-21T20:54:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50552701/sources-steelers-activate-wr-roman-wilson-ir-eagles-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Brooke Pryor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Titans DL Jaylen Harrell hospitalized after car accident in Tampa","description":"Titans defensive lineman Jaylen Harrell was involved in a serious car accident Friday and remains hospitalized, according to the team.","published":"2026-11-21T18:31:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50551434/titans-dl-jaylen-harrell-hospitalized-car-accident-tampa","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Turron Davenport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Raiders' Mark Davis unhappy with 'unfair' image of his father in 'Madden' movie","description":"Saying \"I did the best I could to protect him,\" Raiders owner Mark Davis expressed frustration with the depiction of his father, the late Al Davis, in the new movie \"Madden.\"","published":"2026-11-21T15:27:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50549761/mark-davis-upset-father-portrayal-movie-madden","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football flex and superflex rankings for Week 11","description":"Trying to decide between a couple of closely ranked players this week? Eric Karabell's ranks are here to help.","published":"2026-11-21T14:12:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50507366/fantasy-football-superflex-rankings-2026-qb-rb-wr-te","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Karabell","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Sione Vaki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sione_Vaki","description":"American football player (born 2001)","touched":"2026-11-21T23:11:19Z","intro":"Sione Vaki (born July 30, 2001) is an American professional football running back for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Utah Utes as a two-way player. Vaki was selected by the Lions in the fourth round of the 2024 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Vaki attended Liberty High School in Brentwood, California. In high school, he played on both sides of the ball. On offense he rushed for 401 yards and seven touchdowns, while also bringing in 107 receptions for 2,203 yards and 32 touchdowns. On defense, he notched 142 tackles with one being for a loss, five interceptions, four fumble recoveries, two forced fumbles, and two defensive touchdowns, Vaki also returned a kickoff for a touchdown. Vaki committed to play college football at the University of Utah."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his true freshman season, Vaki totalled 41 tackles with 3.5 going for a loss, three pass deflections, and a forced fumble in the 2022 season.\nIn week one of the 2023 season, he recorded his first career interception versus the Florida Gators. In week seven, Vaki had a breakout game where he played both ways of the ball as he rushed 15 times for 158 yards and two touchdown to help the Utes beat California. In the following week, he rushed nine times for 68 yards, while also hauling in five receptions for 149 yards and two touchdowns, while also notching two tackles and having the best coverage grade on the Utes, as helped them upset USC 34–32.  The rest of the season, the Utes formulated a plan to use Vaki more on offense.\nAs a sophomore, Vaki finished the season with 51 tackles, 8.5 tackles for a loss, two sacks and two interceptions on defense. On offense he had 317 yards rushing (7.5 yards per carry) and two rushing touchdowns. As well as 11 receptions for 203 yards and three receiving touchdowns. He was voted to the first-team All-Pac-12 team twice in 2023, both as a safety and a special teams/all-purpose player. Following the 2023 season, Vaki declared for the 2024 NFL draft after playing two seasons of college football, as he went on a three-year mission trip following his high school graduation."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Vaki was selected in the fourth round, 132nd overall, by the Detroit Lions in the 2024 NFL draft. He was named to the PFWA All-Rookie Team."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Vaki lost his mother Oto’ota due to cancer.  Vaki is a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints; he started to serve a mission for the church in the Nuku'alofa, Tonga, Mission, but was reassigned to the West Salt Lake City, Utah, Mission due to the COVID-19 pandemic."}],"wikidataId":"Q123321999","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4912274","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/V/VakiSi00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/sione-vaki/158505","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/sione-vaki/11740","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sione_Vaki"},"insights":["On the field for 21% of Detroit’s offensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.2M is the 33rd-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2027.","Drafted 132nd overall in 2024 (round 4) by DET."]}